{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/99669-i-just-realized-mummy-had-the-best-5-powers","id":99669,"title":"I just realized, Mummy had the best 5+ Powers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-26T19:49:59-07:00","id":99669,"title":"I just realized, Mummy had the best 5+ Powers","content":"Something odd I just realized, for a mini sub gameline Mummy had the selection of powers over the level five mark. Mage always screwed archspheres up, even screwing up how you raise traits past five making it waaay to convoluted. Vampire was totally hit or miss, with in my impression the majority of Elder powers lamer then the 1-5 powers and more alternate powers, with often horrible horrible rules and thus too expensive. Kueijin suffered the same. Werewolf was pretty good, but many complain some Rank 6 powers or insanely better then others. But Mummy had a good system. It was clean and fun and cool, and they pioneered the Enlightenment trait from the what the company learned from Kueijin and Exalted. I think if Mummy was its own Gameline it would have been fantastic considering their two books in revised feel more complete then say Demon or so, yet they still had room like the 5+ powers of the other Immortals. Demon didn't even get 5+ powers even though their Line had things like Angels/Seraphim and Earthbound/Archdukes/Lucifer!<br /> <br /> Hell I would have loved even more supplements for Mummy because since they hit the essentials with just two books they had a lot of damn room to pad things out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T20:25:56-07:00","id":99688,"title":"","content":"Well, you gotta remember with regards to Garou that there's nothing higher than Rank 6 -- I mean, that's it -- so obviously those few powers at that level are going to be incredibly powerful; there aren't that many of them (not even one for every tribe) and they are literally the only level after 5.<br /> <br /> That said, I would urge you to not discount the crazy awesomeness of Kuei Jin (Kindred of the East) powers. Just go ahead and read the higher levels of Iron Mountain and Black Wind, and tell me that you're not utterly incredulous. I mean, Hell, the KoE have THE best single-target attack power in the WoD: Kiai (or however it's spelled) 6 or 7. You roll some dice pool that could very reasonably be high (it's an attribute and an ability -- not even your Dharma rating which is necessarily going to tend to be lower) at diff 7 (I believe it's diff 7), and you inflict upon your target your Dharma in Aggravated damage for every success scored. That is, if you're using this power you have <i>at least</i> a Dharma of 6; so say you use this power, and score 3 successes (which is doable, believe me), you'd basically inflict 18 health levels of Aggravated damage. Broken.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T20:35:23-07:00","id":99695,"title":"","content":"Powerful and broken is not the same as good. :P Some Kueijin higher powers I like but some didn't have the chops, I mean turning into a tree...<br /> <br /> <br /> I actually like the concept of rank 6 Gifts, and I like them more often then I don't. They are meant to break the rules, do things like make you immortal, steal powers permanently by eating hearts, challenge anyone in the Universe to a Duel. So I'm happy with them, and I have no problem with them being varying in power.<br /> <br /> Just Saying Mummy seems like the culmination in system crunch for Revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T20:50:29-07:00","id":99708,"title":"","content":"Mummy is on a very weird power scale that doesn't really mesh well with our normal expectations of powers. Very few powers in Mummy will directly solve a problem in the same way that powers in other spheres will, and most of the &quot;powers&quot; seem to really be about getting your Attributes to 6+ which is where the best powers come from, not from Hekau. It's actually pretty cool, but it means that it is very difficult to hold Mummy up in comparison to other spheres.<br /> <br /> I'll say for disclosure I really hate Revised Mummy anyway, so take what I say with a pinch of salt (I was a big fan of 2nd ed Mummy and think that they completely destroyed them with the Revised Storyline completely changing what they are).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T07:38:11-07:00","id":100720,"title":"","content":"I actually quite enjoy Revised Mummy, though certain elements were kind of wonky and needed further development (their relationship to the Web of Faith being one that springs to mind). One of my gaming buddies is among the half dozen people on this entire planet of Earth to actually have bought Laws of the Resurrection for LARP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T14:10:12-07:00","id":100872,"title":"","content":"In general I liked the Hekau updates to revised rules I did hate quite a lot of Resurrection which was really disappointing since I absolutely loved 2nd ed Mummy. I hated that they changed who the mummies were, that is instead of playing immortals from Egypt's past we play modern dudes who have a small shard of an ancient Egyptian soul embedded in them, I immensely disliked their decision to part it mechanically and otherwise from Wraith and I absolutely abhorred that their power stat was tied to Humanity 2.0. The strictness of which basically meant that most people likely would have a hard time keeping it at 3-4 range, as loosing it was basically rather easy even if it only happened during a death cycle, and still it cost ridiculously much to raise with xp.<br /> <br /> I'm just glad that MtC returned to ancient immortals angle, even though unfortunately they too tied the memory trait to a morality trait but still it's not nearly as bad as it was with MtR.<br /> <br /> Anyway like I said I liked the Hekau update and do agree that they scale rather nicely even though I do agree with killersquirrel59 on the fact that Mummy powers really do occupy a weird spot on the power scale.<br /> <br /> Demon kinda would have needed 6+ powers even after the power boost given by Mastery background for Earthbound, still I tend to prefer Devil's Due take on Demons and their Arcana are easy to bring on to higher levels since they are kinda made for customizing and adding your own to the mix.<br /> <br /> Kuei-Jin had an extremely solid 1-5 scale but unfortunately the 6+ powers truly did not live up to the expectations created by the 1-5 awesomeness.<br /> <br /> Also just to add about Garou Ranks... There are plenty of small hints that there might be more but at the point a Garou would be achieving them the experience tends to change them to something else, and arguably greater. BSD ranks measure how many layers of the Spiral Labyrinth they have traversed and there are 9 circles in the Labyrinth (Number Two's Incarna status was likely achieved through these means), Kitsune get a new tail for each Rank and there is at least one fox with 9 tails to mention two of the easiest to spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}